      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Single crystals of Ce(HCOO)3 (sample 1) were obtained from a sealed aqueous solution of 1.0 M Ce(IV) in 1.0 M HNO3 / 10.0 M HCOOH (initial pH = 0.8, adjusted with NH3) that underwent slow photoreduction of Ce(IV) to Ce(III). The crystals deposited after 6 months without evaporation under ambient conditions. Direct crystallization from aqueous Ce(III) formate gave only powder. A microcrystalline powder of the same phase (sample P1) was prepared by dissolving 100 mg of CeCl3·7H2O in 10 mL of diethylene glycol monoethyl ether, adding 40 µL of 98–100% formic acid and 200 µL of 25% NH3, washing the white precipitate twice with diethylene glycol monoethyl ether and once with diethyl ether, and drying in air.",
